Message-Id: <8bbee53215a2fe1b7845ec38b3385347f5d6aa41.1791977240.git.dev@kobbler.invalid>
From: Kobbler-Media <dev@kobbler.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:14:47 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] android: display: release the window surface on close

The vout keeps its window when the player saves it for the next video,
and the app may set a new surface on it in between. Without releasing
the cached ANativeWindow, the next display opens on the dead surface:
ASurfaceControl creation fails and the GL fallback cannot connect.

The OpenGL and Vulkan displays already release it on close.
---
 modules/video_output/android/display.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/video_output/android/display.c b/modules/video_output/android/display.c
index ca50379bd7..8510ff3086 100644
--- a/modules/video_output/android/display.c
+++ b/modules/video_output/android/display.c
@@ -639,6 +639,12 @@ static void Close(vout_display_t *vd)
     if (sys->sub.window != NULL)
         subpicture_CloseDisplay(vd);
 
+    /* The window outlives the display when the player keeps it for the next
+     * video, and the app may hand it a new surface in between: the next
+     * display must fetch the surface again rather than reuse a dead one. */
+    AWindowHandler_releaseANativeWindow(sys->awh, AWindow_Video);
+    AWindowHandler_releaseANativeWindow(sys->awh, AWindow_Subtitles);
+
     free(sys);
 }
 
